        {
          "page": "2",
          "section": "2. Experimental methods",
          "quote": "The Nb45Ta25Ti15Hf15 RHEA was fabricated by arc-melting high-purity elemental refractory metals. The feedstock slugs and wires were all 99.95 % + purity by metals basis. Contamination during the arc-melting process was limited by pulling a vacuum of 1 × 10-5 torr on the chamber and then backfilling it with commercial purity Ar. Additionally, a Ti getter was melted in the chamber for 2 min before melting the Nb45Ta25Ti15Hf15 alloys to remove any residual O2, N2, and H2O from the chamber and minimize interstitial impurities in the as-cast alloys. The arc-melted buttons were flipped and remelted five times without breaking the inert atmosphere to promote homogeneity.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "fbbcf0babdd500aa:part:001"
        },
